Reason:
The `tmp` buffer is allocated with `kcalloc()` but the error handling path for a failed `acpi_evaluate_dsm()` call (when it returns NULL) directly returns an error without freeing `tmp`. This causes a memory leak because the allocated memory is no longer referenced.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
<text>
if (!obj) {
    kfree(tmp);
    return -EINVAL;
}
</text>
Reason:
The fix adds explicit deallocation of the `tmp` buffer via `kfree(tmp)` before returning the error when `acpi_evaluate_dsm()` fails. This ensures that the allocated memory is freed in the error path, preventing the memory leak.

